1
00:00:00,450 --> 00:00:01,350
A mango.

2
00:00:01,187 --> 00:00:02,087
A coconut.

3
00:00:02,020 --> 00:00:03,398
A soaked gram seed.

4
00:00:03,798 --> 00:00:07,374
A juicy mango and a hard, hairy
coconut look nothing alike.

5
00:00:07,374 --> 00:00:10,443
Yet botanists put them in
the same group of fruits.

6
00:00:10,893 --> 00:00:12,786
Diya spotted both in the kitchen.

7
00:00:12,786 --> 00:00:16,730
She wants to be a doctor, and she
asked: how can these two be the same

8
00:00:16,730 --> 00:00:17,677
kind of fruit?

9
00:00:18,027 --> 00:00:22,681
The answer is in how a fruit is built,
layer by layer, and what hides inside

10
00:00:22,681 --> 00:00:23,581
its seed.

11
00:00:23,942 --> 00:00:28,014
By the end, you will name the layers
of a fruit, and the parts of a gram

12
00:00:28,014 --> 00:00:29,435
seed and a maize grain.

13
00:00:30,085 --> 00:00:31,609
First, what is a fruit?

14
00:00:31,959 --> 00:00:35,708
After fertilisation, the
ovary of a flower ripens.

15
00:00:35,708 --> 00:00:38,544
A fruit is a mature, ripened ovary.

16
00:00:38,994 --> 00:00:41,267
The ovules inside it become the seeds.

17
00:00:41,267 --> 00:00:45,370
So the fruit comes from the ovary,
and each seed comes from an ovule.

18
00:00:45,820 --> 00:00:50,951
If a fruit forms without fertilisation,
it is called a parthenocarpic fruit.

19
00:00:50,951 --> 00:00:52,573
Banana is an example.

20
00:00:53,223 --> 00:00:56,616
Let's zoom into a mango,
one level at a time.

21
00:00:56,966 --> 00:01:00,786
A fruit has a wall, called the
pericarp, and seeds inside.

22
00:01:00,786 --> 00:01:02,053
Peri means around.

23
00:01:02,053 --> 00:01:03,272
Carp means fruit.

24
00:01:03,772 --> 00:01:04,682
Cut it open.

25
00:01:04,682 --> 00:01:08,002
When the wall is thick and
fleshy, it has three layers.

26
00:01:08,502 --> 00:01:10,945
The thin outer skin is the epicarp.

27
00:01:10,945 --> 00:01:13,963
The thick juicy part
we eat is the mesocarp.

28
00:01:13,963 --> 00:01:16,144
The hard stone is the endocarp.

29
00:01:16,644 --> 00:01:18,754
Inside the stone sits one seed.

30
00:01:18,754 --> 00:01:23,386
A mango grows from an ovary with one
carpel, sitting above the other flower

31
00:01:23,386 --> 00:01:24,286
parts.

32
00:01:23,983 --> 00:01:27,110
A one seeded fruit like
this is called a drupe.

33
00:01:27,760 --> 00:01:29,985
Now watch a flower turn into a fruit.

34
00:01:30,335 --> 00:01:31,235
Step one.

35
00:01:31,109 --> 00:01:35,266
The flower is pollinated, and
fertilisation happens inside its ovule.

36
00:01:36,016 --> 00:01:36,916
Step two.

37
00:01:36,681 --> 00:01:39,105
The petals and stamens
dry up and fall away.

38
00:01:39,105 --> 00:01:40,232
Their job is done.

39
00:01:40,982 --> 00:01:41,882
Step three.

40
00:01:41,861 --> 00:01:44,855
The ovary swells, and
grows bigger and bigger.

41
00:01:45,605 --> 00:01:46,505
Step four.

42
00:01:46,348 --> 00:01:49,731
The ovary wall becomes the
pericarp, the wall of the fruit.

43
00:01:50,481 --> 00:01:51,381
Step five.

44
00:01:51,231 --> 00:01:53,224
The ovule inside becomes the seed.

45
00:01:53,224 --> 00:01:54,560
Now we have a fruit.

46
00:01:55,310 --> 00:01:56,646
Now open a seed.

47
00:01:56,646 --> 00:01:59,565
Start with a gram seed, soaked overnight.

48
00:01:59,915 --> 00:02:02,027
The outer cover is the seed coat.

49
00:02:02,027 --> 00:02:05,496
It has two layers, the outer
testa and the inner tegmen.

50
00:02:05,996 --> 00:02:10,326
The hilum is a scar, where the
seed was attached to the fruit.

51
00:02:10,326 --> 00:02:13,489
Just above it is a tiny
pore, the micropyle.

52
00:02:13,989 --> 00:02:16,494
Inside is the embryo, the baby plant.

53
00:02:16,494 --> 00:02:20,670
It has an embryonal axis and two
cotyledons, fat with stored food.

54
00:02:21,170 --> 00:02:24,843
At one end of the axis is
the radicle, the future root.

55
00:02:24,843 --> 00:02:28,160
At the other end is the
plumule, the future shoot.

56
00:02:28,810 --> 00:02:30,066
Now a maize grain.

57
00:02:30,066 --> 00:02:33,609
Here the seed coat is thin,
and joined to the fruit wall.

58
00:02:34,109 --> 00:02:37,649
Most of the grain is
endosperm, a big food store.

59
00:02:37,649 --> 00:02:41,013
A protein layer, the
aleurone layer, wraps it.

60
00:02:41,513 --> 00:02:44,448
The embryo is small,
in a groove at one end.

61
00:02:44,448 --> 00:02:47,225
Its one cotyledon is
large and shield shaped.

62
00:02:47,225 --> 00:02:48,995
It is called the scutellum.

63
00:02:49,495 --> 00:02:52,660
The plumule sits in a sheath
called the coleoptile.

64
00:02:52,660 --> 00:02:55,824
The radicle sits in a sheath
called the coleorhiza.

65
00:02:56,474 --> 00:02:57,456
Side by side.

66
00:02:57,456 --> 00:02:58,991
Gram has two cotyledons.

67
00:02:58,991 --> 00:03:00,899
Maize has one, the scutellum.

68
00:03:01,649 --> 00:03:05,943
In gram, bean and pea, the endosperm
is used up before the seed is ripe.

69
00:03:05,943 --> 00:03:07,852
These seeds are non endospermous.

70
00:03:07,852 --> 00:03:10,879
Maize keeps a bulky endosperm,
so it is endospermic.

71
00:03:11,629 --> 00:03:16,793
Only the maize embryo wraps its plumule
and radicle in sheaths, the coleoptile

72
00:03:16,793 --> 00:03:18,269
and the coleorhiza.

73
00:03:19,019 --> 00:03:19,919
Your turn.

74
00:03:19,812 --> 00:03:22,165
A coconut is a drupe, like a mango.

75
00:03:22,165 --> 00:03:24,326
But its middle layer is not juicy.

76
00:03:24,326 --> 00:03:27,034
Is the coconut's mesocarp
fleshy, or fibrous?

77
00:03:27,034 --> 00:03:28,156
Pause and think.

78
00:03:31,356 --> 00:03:32,256
Fibrous!

79
00:03:32,081 --> 00:03:35,133
The hairy husk of a
coconut is its mesocarp.

80
00:03:35,133 --> 00:03:38,604
Same three layers as a
mango, so both are drupes.

81
00:03:39,254 --> 00:03:40,154
Remember this.

82
00:03:40,094 --> 00:03:41,624
The ovary becomes the fruit.

83
00:03:41,624 --> 00:03:43,115
The ovule becomes the seed.

84
00:03:43,715 --> 00:03:45,293
Now, a worked example.

85
00:03:45,293 --> 00:03:46,193
Six parts.

86
00:03:46,106 --> 00:03:49,767
Did each one come from the
ovary wall, or from the ovule?

87
00:03:50,117 --> 00:03:52,314
Mango flesh is the mesocarp.

88
00:03:52,314 --> 00:03:53,350
Ovary wall.

89
00:03:53,800 --> 00:03:56,404
The gram cotyledons
are part of the embryo.

90
00:03:56,404 --> 00:03:57,304
Ovule.

91
00:03:57,406 --> 00:04:00,163
The hard mango stone is the endocarp.

92
00:04:00,163 --> 00:04:01,454
Ovary wall too.

93
00:04:01,904 --> 00:04:04,621
The hilum is a scar on the seed coat.

94
00:04:04,621 --> 00:04:05,521
Ovule.

95
00:04:05,699 --> 00:04:08,668
The coconut husk is the fibrous mesocarp.

96
00:04:08,668 --> 00:04:09,672
Ovary wall.

97
00:04:10,122 --> 00:04:13,275
And the maize scutellum
is its one cotyledon.

98
00:04:13,275 --> 00:04:14,175
Ovule.

99
00:04:14,570 --> 00:04:16,032
Now, the exam trap.

100
00:04:16,382 --> 00:04:19,390
Many students think the hard
mango stone is the seed.

101
00:04:19,790 --> 00:04:24,066
But the stone is the endocarp,
the inner layer of the fruit wall.

102
00:04:24,066 --> 00:04:26,477
The real seed sits inside the stone.

103
00:04:27,127 --> 00:04:28,266
Where is this asked?

104
00:04:28,266 --> 00:04:31,889
As statement questions on the parts of
a seed, and as matching fruit layers

105
00:04:31,889 --> 00:04:32,789
with examples.

106
00:04:33,307 --> 00:04:34,419
Exam level now.

107
00:04:34,419 --> 00:04:36,249
Which statements are correct?

108
00:04:36,249 --> 00:04:37,408
Pause and solve.

109
00:04:42,808 --> 00:04:44,101
The answer is A.

110
00:04:44,101 --> 00:04:45,795
Statements one and four.

111
00:04:46,295 --> 00:04:47,195
Two is wrong.

112
00:04:47,167 --> 00:04:48,864
Pea seeds are non endospermous.

113
00:04:48,864 --> 00:04:49,817
Three is wrong.

114
00:04:49,817 --> 00:04:51,635
The coleoptile covers the plumule.

115
00:04:52,135 --> 00:04:56,942
The scutellum is the one cotyledon
of maize, and the coconut mesocarp is

116
00:04:56,942 --> 00:04:57,842
fibrous.

117
00:04:58,295 --> 00:04:59,835
Here is your recap.

118
00:04:59,835 --> 00:05:01,418
Screenshot this card.

119
00:05:04,618 --> 00:05:06,804
Can you answer these three
questions without help?

120
00:05:07,204 --> 00:05:08,104
One.

121
00:05:07,642 --> 00:05:10,476
Name the three layers of
the pericarp in a mango.

122
00:05:11,376 --> 00:05:12,276
Two.

123
00:05:11,764 --> 00:05:13,567
What are the testa and the tegmen?

124
00:05:14,467 --> 00:05:15,367
Three.

125
00:05:15,015 --> 00:05:17,825
What do the coleoptile
and the coleorhiza cover?

126
00:05:18,925 --> 00:05:23,333
Next time: can a whole flower be written
in one short line, like a formula?

127
00:05:23,333 --> 00:05:26,488
We find out in floral formula
and the family Solanaceae.
